WEBVTT - Module 2: Alarm Sounds & Safety Leadership

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.500
Hey, welcome! Today we're talking about how knowing fire safety makes you a real leader.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.200
So what does a hero actually do in an emergency? Well, they don't panic — they have a plan!

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.200
Take Gabriel for example. When he saw a fire at his friend's house, he knew exactly what to do.

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.500
He called for help right away and kept everyone calm. You can be a leader like him, too!

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.500
First things first: to be a leader, you've got to know your enemy. Let's learn fire's secret recipe.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
It's called the Fire Triangle. It's super simple: Heat, Fuel, and Oxygen.

7
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.000
Take one away, and the fire goes out!

8
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.200
First, you need Heat — think of a spark, a flame, anything hot enough to ignite.

9
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.000
Then you have Fuel — anything that can burn like wood, paper, you name it. It's the fire's food!

10
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.000
And finally, Oxygen. Fire breathes just like we do, and it's all around us in the air.

11
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:59.000
And things happen fast — a tiny flame can turn into a whole room on fire in minutes!

12
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:05.500
This is exactly why matches and lighters are not toys. They're tools for adults for making heat.

13
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.500
Okay, so you know about fire, but at school, how do you know when it's a real emergency?

14
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.500
You've got to know the difference! A regular bell means change class.

15
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.500
A fire alarm is loud, non-stop, and means: GET OUT!

16
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.200
And that red box on the wall? Pulling that switch triggers the alarm for the entire school.

17
00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.200
When that alarm goes off, it's go time! This is your moment to be a leader.

18
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.500
What do you do? Stay calm, walk — don't run, and stick with your buddy. No one gets left behind!

19
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.200
A few pro tips: If there's smoke, stay low! And always check doors for heat before opening.

20
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:49.000
Following these rules shows real integrity. You're not just protecting yourself, you're protecting everyone!

21
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.500
So there you have it: you know the Fire Triangle, you know the alarms, and you know the plan.

22
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.500
Remember this: safety isn't just about rules, it's really an act of leadership!

23
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.000
How are you going to be a safety leader today? Go out and make a difference!
